<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Somewhere in Afrika (Manfred Mann's Earth Band)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1983</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Get on the Bus soundtrack (Stevie Wonder)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Psychedelicatessen (Moodswings, with Tanita Tikaram)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">medley with &quot;Oh Happy Day&quot;</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Streetcore (Joe Strummer and the Mescaleros)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, released after Strummer's death</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Unearthed (Johnny Cash and Joe Strummer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">duet cover, recorded in the American IV sessions</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The North Star (Remedy Drive)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2018</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Speech of Marcus Garvey at Menelik Hall, Sydney, Nova Scotia, published in Black Man</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1937</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of some key lines</span></li></ul></section>
